      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is wise to be cautious with high doses of supplements, as too much magnesium can cause digestive upset, like diarrhea. A dose of 600mg to 800mg of magnesium citrate is quite high for a standard nightly dose, and you should check the specific instructions on your product. Before taking such a large amount, I highly recommend consulting with your primary care physician to ensure it's safe for your individual health profile.",
